        "DateText": "1665-1678/79",
        "Notes": "The Academy was first held at Sampieri`s house, and subsequently at Montanari`s house. After Montanari`s departure from Bologna, it was probably hosted by Cardinal Davia for a short time. Details can be found in Salvatore Rotta, `Scienza e pubblica felicit\u00e0 in Geminiano Montanari`, in Miscellanea Seicento Firenze Le Monnier 1971 pp. 97 and 165-6. This Academy was followed by the Accademia degli Inquieti, see M. Cavazza, `Dal \"Coro anatomico\" agli \"Inquieti\", in Quaderni storici (1981). See also Ivano Dal Prete`s biography of Montanari, in DBI.",
